<!--
  Xn handover (inter-gNB, Xn interface), rfsim, 5x ping-pong between two gNBs.

  Deployment: ci-scripts/yaml_files/5g_rfsimulator_xn_ho/docker-compose.yaml
    Open5GS 5GC (NGAP Path Switch is not supported by the OAI 5GC) + two gNBs
    in CU-CP/CU-UP/DU split, peered over Xn:
      gNB-0  gNB_ID 0xe00  PCI 0  CU-CP 192.168.71.150  DU 192.168.71.171 (gNB_DU_ID 3584)
      gNB-1  gNB_ID 0xb00  PCI 1  CU-CP 192.168.71.180  DU 192.168.71.182 (gNB_DU_ID 1234)
    one rfsim NR-UE (192.168.71.190), telnet CI shell "ci" on CU-CP :9090.

  Each hop: "ci trigger_xn_ho <target PCI>,<UE id>" on the source CU-CP, then
  check_xn_ho.sh checks every step in the CU-CP logs:
    XnAP Handover Request/Ack, RRCReconfiguration (HO command), SN Status Transfer,
    RRCReconfigurationComplete, NGAP Path Switch Request/Ack, XnAP UE Context Release.
  The UE then has to be on the target DU, and ping/iperf have to pass.
-->

